## COMMUNICATION
## Entry for the Table of Contents
We present heterogeneous hollow multi-shelled structures (HoMSs) by controllably evolving the metal organic frameworks (MOFs)-based coating layer into heterogeneous casings on surface of the original HoMSs. By a two-step calcination process, \(\mathsf{S n O}_{2}@\mathsf{F e}_{2}\mathsf{O}_{3}\) (MOF)-HoMSs electrodes demonstrate superior lithium storage capacity and cycling stability to original \(\mathsf{S n O}_{2}\)-HoMSs, which can be attributed to the topological features of the MOFs evolutive casing.
Hollow Multi-Shelled Structure with Metal Organic Frameworks Evolutive Heterogeneous Casing for Enhanced Lithium Storage
